The original LICENSE and source notices are preserved.

Pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi)
Copyright Mario Zechner. Licensed under MIT.
The packaged application contains Pi's license and dependency notices under
Resources/aionpi-runtime. Pi is built from the user's local fork.

Node.js and its included libraries are distributed with their original LICENSE
under Resources/aionpi-runtime/node/LICENSE.

Mu / @kyrn/judge (https://github.com/qybaihe/mu)
Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner. Licensed under MIT.
The Jev System One wire protocol adapter and three-zone decision policy in this
integration are adapted from @kyrn/judge. Mu branding, memory, hive, swarm, and
collaboration implementations are not included.

Cua Driver (https://github.com/trycua/cua)
Copyright Cua AI, Inc. Licensed under MIT.
Cua Driver is an external, separately installed dependency. It is not bundled
with TheOne. The optional cua-perception extension is not installed or used.

Jev-cu (https://github.com/Sac-Y/Jev-cu)
Copyright (c) 2026 Sac-Y. Licensed under MIT.
The fast desktop observation/selection/execution loop references Jev-cu's
driver separation and bounded task/resource handoff design. TheOne retains
its existing Cua Driver rather than importing Codex's proprietary runtime.

Jev Ultrafast (https://github.com/browser-use/jev-ultrafast)
Copyright (c) 2026 Browser Use. Licensed under MIT.
The operation-specific target choices and single-request decision validation
are adapted to native desktop controls from Jev Ultrafast's model.py.

